 New Roman,Times"></font>
</p><p><a name=3D"11.2"></a><b><font face=3D"Times New Roman,Times">11.2 No=
n-Blocking
Assignment</font></b><font face=3D"Times New Roman,Times"></font>
</p><p><font face=3D"Times New Roman,Times">Allows scheduling of assignments
with out blocking the procedural flow. Blocking assignmets allow timing
control which are delays whereas , non-blocking assignments permit timing
control which can be delays or event contol. Th non-blocking assignment
is used to avoid race conditions and can model RTL assignments.</font>
<br><font face=3D"Times New Roman,Times"></font>&nbsp;
</p><center><table width=3D"80%" cellspacing=3D"0" cellpadding=3D"0" border=
=3D"1" bgcolor=3D"#ffffff">
<tbody><tr>
<td>
<pre><font face=3D"Times New Roman,Times">/* assume a =3D 10, b =3D 20, c=
 =3D 30, d =3D 40 at the start of block */

always @ (posedge clk)
&nbsp;&nbsp; begin: block
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; a &lt;=3D #10 b;
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; b &lt;=3D #10 c;
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; c &lt;=3D #10 d;

/* at the end of the block + 10 time units, a =3D 20, b =3D 30, c =3D 40 */=
</font></pre>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table></center>
